title: Microsoft Hyper-V VM: Checkpoints
agents: windows
catalog: os/virtual
license: GPLv2
distribution: check_mk
description:
 This check monitors the checkpoints (snapshots) of a virtual machine running
 on Microsoft Hyper-V. It shows the number of checkpoints and the age of the
 latest and the oldest checkpoint.

 By default the check is {WARN} if the oldest checkpoint is older than 10 days
 and {CRIT} if it is older than 20 days. The age of the latest checkpoint has no
 levels by default. Both levels are configured with the rule
 "Hyper-V VM checkpoints".

 The check is {OK} if the VM has no checkpoints and {UNKNOWN} if no creation
 date of a checkpoint can be read.

 The data is collected by the agent plug-in {hyperv_host.ps1}, which can be
 deployed with the agent bakery rule "Hyper-V". The plug-in sends the data
 as piggyback data to a host with the name of the VM.

discovery:
 One service is created on the piggyback host of each VM, also if the VM has
 no checkpoints.
